      "claim_id": "innodb-clustered-key-selection",
      "text": "For MySQL 8.4 InnoDB, the clustered index stores row data; InnoDB uses PRIMARY KEY when present, otherwise the first all-NOT-NULL UNIQUE index, otherwise a hidden generated clustered index.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql84-innodb-clustered-secondary"],
      "answer_locations": ["核心结论", "1 分钟版", "3 分钟版", "关键细节", "原理机制", "常见追问", "易错点"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "innodb-secondary-primary-key-lookup",
      "text": "In MySQL 8.4 InnoDB, a secondary-index record contains the indexed columns and primary-key columns; InnoDB uses the primary-key value to locate the row through the clustered index, and long primary keys enlarge secondary indexes.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql84-innodb-clustered-secondary"],
      "answer_locations": ["核心结论", "1 分钟版", "3 分钟版", "关键细节", "原理机制", "常见追问", "易错点"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "innodb-clustered-access-boundary",
      "text": "The MySQL 8.4 documentation states that clustered-index lookup leads directly to the page containing row data and can save an I/O relative to a different storage organization; this is an InnoDB storage-organization statement, not a universal performance guarantee.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql84-innodb-clustered-secondary"],
      "answer_locations": ["3 分钟版", "关键细节", "原理机制", "易错点"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "mysql-covering-index-and-order-boundaries",
      "text": "MySQL 8.4 defines a covering index as one providing all necessary query results from the index tree; it also states that index-based sorting/grouping requires a usable index leftmost prefix and compatible direction, while each additional index adds insert, update, and delete maintenance cost.",
